  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "(b) Given $x=a \\sin \\theta$ and $y=b \\cos \\theta$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{d x}{d \\theta}=a \\cos \\theta$ and $\\frac{d y}{d \\theta}=-b \\sin \\theta$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{d y}{d \\theta} \\times \\frac{d \\theta}{d x}=-\\frac{b}{a} \\tan \\theta \\Rightarrow \\frac{d^{2} y}{d x^{2}}=\\frac{-b}{a} \\sec ^{2} \\theta$",
    "image": null
  },
